ct gloss identifies Rav Kahana from Babylonia as the referent of that one of yours. The identification of the addressee as the second Chizkiyah is inferred in Heilprin and Rashba.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Gittin 84b:10:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Gittin_84b.10.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1213:1:citation-22","he":[1615,1643],"en":[2729,2744],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_84b.10.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 84b:10:1","assessment":"Tosafot proposes that Yochanan said it to his Babylonian students. Preserve this as a separate interpretation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 84b:10:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_84b.10.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1213:1:citation-23","he":[1731,1756],"en":[2967,2992],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Avodah_Zarah_16a.1"},"reference":"Rif Avodah Zarah 16a:1","assessment":"The Rif records the ruling and student–teacher principle at the beginning of this page.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rif Avodah Zarah 16a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Avodah_Zarah_16a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,6,7,9,10,11,12,14,15,17,18,19,20,21,22],"holds":[{"raw":"היוחסין אות י' כתב להיפך","reason":"The accessible Wikisource transcription stops before yod. Searches of the Daat and Tartu OCR did not confirm this exact report. Preserve Heilprin’s attribution.","evidence":[]},{"raw":"חזקיה נגמרה צורתו","reason":"Shalshelet’s comparison is to the other twin’s birth. Niddah and Yevamot leave open which emerged first. The inference from name order and burial placement belongs to Heilprin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 27a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_27a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 65b:17","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_65b.17"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shalshelet HaKabbalah 32b as cited by Heilprin, Chiyya twins notice","target":{"url":"https://www.scribd.com/document/698244685/%D7%A9%D7%9C%D7%A9%D7%9C%D7%AA-%D7%94%D7%A7%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%94"},"witness":"Shalshelet HaKabbalah, digitized Hebrew OCR"}]},{"raw":"והיה רבו של ר' יוחנן (ע\"ש)","reason":"Shabbat attests the teacher address. No unique internal destination in the Yochanan group is admitted from this bare pointer.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 112b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_112b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"וחגיגה (ח' א', ט' א')","reason":"Chagigah 8a concerns the disputed offerings. At 9a the named Chizkiyah statement concerns ritual impurity. Leave the separate 9a association qualified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chagigah 8a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_8a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 9a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_9a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"מר' יהודה נשיאה","reason":"The checked Tosafot reads Yehudah HaNasi. Keep the Warsaw title Nesia in Heilprin’s account.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Avodah Zarah 38b:7:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Avodah_Zarah_38b.7.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"תיבת רבי ט\"ס כי לא נסמכו","reason":"The checked Bavli has Rabbi in the question and in the teacher address. Heilprin’s proposed correction remains attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 112b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_112b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 112b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_112b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"חזקיה בריה דר' חייא בריה דרב כהנא","reason":"The checked Rashba has Chiyya son of Rav without Kahana. The Bavli has bare Chizkiyah. Preserve Heilprin’s patronymic and his express nonfinding.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashba on Gittin 84b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashba_on_Gittin_84b.1"},"witness":"Gerlitz edition, published by Oraita"},{"reference":"Gittin 84b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_84b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ס' תחלת חכמה דף נ\"א ד'","reason":"Exact title occurrence, pagination and the source of the reported formulation need bibliographical collation.","evidence":[]},{"raw":"כתב בנ\"ח בי\"ד סי' קמ\"ה","reason":"The abbreviation and exact text at section 145 lack a securely matched work. A check of the candidate Bach passage did not substantiate the quotation.","evidence":[]},{"raw":"וכתב היבין שמועה","reason":"Work is named in the received text, but the exact passage and transmission through the abbreviated source remain unconfirmed.","evidence":[]}],"notes":[{"text":"Niddah and Yevamot leave the first birth unnamed. Shalshelet’s comparison is to Yehudah’s birth. Seniority from name order or burial placement is Heilprin’s inference. Rashi on Berakhot glosses the brothers’ lapse as forgetting their learning. At Gittin, the checked Rashba gives a second Chizkiyah, with the patronymic Chiyya son of Rav. Heilprin’s text includes Kahana and explicitly questions the identification. Keep the two explanations of who heard Yochanan’s statement, and the Rif’s ruling on the teacher–student relationship.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 27a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_27a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Niddah 27a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_27a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 65b:17","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_65b.17"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 65b:1